  "generatedAt": "2026-10-11T12:14:17.585Z",
  "title": "Builder-family detection, fail-closed reviews, and diff-aware posting",
  "summary": "This change reworks how osf decides which model family built a change, and what it does when it cannot tell. `builder::family_of` now scans every word (and every `/`-separated part) of a `Code-Generator:` trailer's model name against a single shared table in `agents::MODEL_FAMILIES`, so vendor-first names like `Anthropic Claude Code claude-sonnet-5-5` resolve the same as `Claude Sonnet 5.5`; a name whose words point at two families is `unknown` rather than guessed. Detection is now per-commit: a clean merge with no trailer is exempt, but any other commit with no trailer (or an unrecognised one) makes the builder family unknown, and the run fails closed — no reviewer counts, the outcome is could-not-run, and the reason quotes the offending trailer. Reviewers left out for family now record `not_run` in their saved run and a note in the posted summary. Separately, `review::DiffLines` parses `gh pr diff` so that findings outside the pull request's diff are posted in the review body instead of as inline comments (which GitHub rejects with HTTP 422), with the body trimmed and the overflow counted rather than refusing the review.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
